comment_B:
SetCategoryAxisReverseOrder uses ReplaceChild(scaling, new Orientation…), but ReplaceChild in this class removes and appends, which can put <c:orientation> after <c:logBase>/<c:max>/<c:min> if they already exist. That can violate the required <c:scaling> child element order and be ignored by Office. Consider normalizing the scaling children order (or inserting orientation at the correct position) after updating it.
```suggestion

 // Ensure the orientation element exists and is in the correct position:
 // <c:logBase>?, <c:orientation>?, <c:max>?, <c:min>?, <c:majorUnit>?, <c:minorUnit>?
 C.Orientation? orientation = scaling.GetFirstChild<C.Orientation>();
 if (orientation == null) {
 orientation = new C.Orientation {
 Val = reverseOrder ? C.OrientationValues.MaxMin : C.OrientationValues.MinMax
 };

 // Insert after any existing logBase, but before other scaling children.
 OpenXmlElement? insertBefore = null;
 foreach (OpenXmlElement child in scaling.Elements()) {
 if (child is not C.LogBase) {
 insertBefore = child;
 break;
 }
 }

 if (insertBefore != null) {
 scaling.InsertBefore(orientation, insertBefore);
 } else {
 scaling.AppendChild(orientation);
 }
 } else {
 orientation.Val = reverseOrder ? C.OrientationValues.MaxMin : C.OrientationValues.MinMax;
 }
```

