comment_A:
ETagCache and prCache are instantiated inside enrichSessionsPRBatch(), so they reset on every call. This means (1) ETags never persist across polling cycles, and (2) prCache is always empty at the time you decide whether to refresh, so most/all PRs will refresh every run. To get the intended rate-limit reduction, these caches need to live across invocations (e.g., module-level singletons or stored on the SCM instance and reused).
```suggestion
const etagCache = new ETagCache();
const prCache = new LRUCache<string, { success: boolean; enrichment: PREnrichmentData }>(
 ENRICHMENT_CACHE_SIZE,
);

export async function enrichSessionsPRBatch(
 prs: PRInfo[],
 config?: { project?: unknown; observer?: BatchObserver },
): Promise<Map<string, PREnrichmentData>> {
 const observer = config?.observer ?? new BatchObserverImpl("rest-parallel");
```

