The current implementation disables all standard ligatures for Turkish locale by setting "liga" to 0. This is overly broad and may disable other legitimate ligatures in Turkish text. Consider using more specific OpenType feature tags like "ffi" or explicitly disabling only the problematic ligatures while preserving others that are appropriate for Turkish.
```suggestion
 // Turkish locale: avoid problematic ligatures without disabling all
 // standard ligatures. In Turkish, the dotless i (ı) is a separate letter,
 // and certain ligatures (e.g., "fi") can be undesirable, but disabling
 // the entire "liga" feature is overly broad and may remove legitimate
 // ligatures. Prefer disabling only discretionary/historical ligatures.
 if (strncmp(lang, "tr", 2) == 0 &&
 (lang[2] == '\0' || lang[2] == '-' || lang[2] == '_')) {
 text_style.addFontFeature(SkString("dlig"), 0);
 text_style.addFontFeature(SkString("hlig"), 0);
```

