The new public setter allows assigning `_speakers` with arbitrary keys. `addChunk` assumes all keys are within `0..<config.numSpeakers` (e.g. it writes into `confirmedCounts[index]`), so negative or out-of-range keys will cause an index-out-of-bounds crash. Consider validating/filtering the incoming dictionary (and potentially reconciling each `DiarizerSpeaker.index` with its slot) before assignment, and using a barrier-synchronized write consistent with the rest of the class’ mutation patterns.
```suggestion
 set {
 let maxSpeakers = config.numSpeakers
 let filteredSpeakers: [Int: DiarizerSpeaker]

 if maxSpeakers > 0 {
 let validRange = 0 ..< maxSpeakers
 filteredSpeakers = newValue.filter { (key, _) in
 validRange.contains(key)
 }
 } else {
 filteredSpeakers = [:]
 }

 queue.async(flags: .barrier) {
 self._speakers = filteredSpeakers
 }
 }
```

