comment_B:
The `git worktree list` call checks only the returned `err`, but `internal/command.Executor.Execute` always returns a nil error and surfaces command failures via `ExecutionResult.Results[i].Error`. As a result, if `git worktree list` fails, this code will likely proceed with empty output and return `WorktreeNotFound` instead of a `GitCommandFailed`-style error. Please check `len(result.Results)` and `result.Results[0].Error` (and include any `Output`) before parsing.
```suggestion
 if len(result.Results) == 0 {
 return errors.GitCommandFailed("git worktree list", "empty execution result")
 }

 gitResult := result.Results[0]
 if gitResult.Error != nil {
 msg := gitResult.Error.Error()
 if gitResult.Output != "" {
 msg = msg + ": " + gitResult.Output
 }
 return errors.GitCommandFailed("git worktree list", msg)
 }

 worktrees := parseWorktreesFromOutput(gitResult.Output)
```

