comment_A:
`HighlightSequenceInline.RenderMarkdown()` delegates to `Inlines.RenderMarkdown()`, but `TextRun.RenderMarkdown()` does not escape '='. This can generate ambiguous/invalid output when highlighted content contains `==` (e.g., from source `==a\==b==`), because the re-rendered Markdown can prematurely close/reopen highlight. Consider rendering highlight sequences with highlight-aware escaping for plain text nodes (escape '=' in `TextRun` segments, similar to how `HighlightInline` uses `EscapeHighlightText`) while still allowing nested formatting nodes to render normally.
```suggestion
 internal string RenderMarkdown() {
 var innerMarkdown = Inlines.RenderMarkdown();
 // Escape '=' inside highlighted content so it cannot be misinterpreted
 // as a highlight delimiter when re-rendered as Markdown.
 innerMarkdown = innerMarkdown.Replace("=", "\\=");
 return "==" + innerMarkdown + "==";
 }
```

